WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.600
What patients decide at home, the clinic rarely sees.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:13.600
18% of supplement users had told a provider. 23,005 U.S. emergency visits a year from supplements.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:19.200
Ladder closes the loop: Capture → Share → Interpret → Act → Close the loop.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.000
Meet Alex, 37. Type 2 diabetes. He takes metformin.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.000
A video tells him berberine is “nature’s Ozempic.”

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Before acting on it, he checks it with Ladder.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.200
Ladder shows what the studies found, and where the video stretched them.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.600
It never tells him to stop his medicine.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:50.400
Alex plans to start berberine and stop metformin.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:54.000
Normally, his clinic would never hear about this.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.600
Ladder asks: want your care team to know?

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:02.200
He joins his clinic’s study on the JupyterHealth Exchange.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.400
His medicines and labs come from his patient portal, with permission.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.400
Sent, with his consent.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:13.600
Behind the scenes: FHIR data on the Exchange, addressed to Dr. Lee’s team.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:19.200
Our open question for Edge Medicine: store “considering” as a MedicationStatement or an Observation?

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.000
The next day, Dr. Lee opens Alex’s chart.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.400
No supplements on record. But Ladder has a new signal.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.000
One card: his words, the evidence, his medicines and A1c.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.600
No AI advice. The clinician decides.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.200
Dr. Lee replies.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.600
Alex hears back three days after his decision, not at his next visit.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.200
The loop is closed.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:02:00.200
A claim nobody has reviewed yet?

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:05.200
Ladder gives no verdict until a licensed expert reviews it.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:11.400
And if Alex says no, nothing reaches the clinic.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:19.200
Three JupyterHealth pieces: Exchange, Voilà on JupyterHub, SMART on FHIR.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:26.800
Phase 1 tests one question: will patients tell their care team?

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:36.000
Ladder. Decided at home, seen in clinic.
